// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6229 new: SSH Authorized Keys Made Immutable
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6229
// Pull request author: marvalous123
// Change: new rule
// Title: SSH Authorized Keys Made Immutable
// Sigma ID: 93e19118-a707-468d-affb-691892eed63c
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Mark C (Atlas SOC Lab)
// Date: 2026-08-14 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1222.002
// Description: Detects use of the chattr utility to add immutable or append-only attributes to an SSH
//   authorized_keys file. Threat actors may use this after planting a public key to make their
//   persistence harder to remove.
// False positives:
//   - Administrators intentionally protecting approved SSH authorized_keys files
//   - Configuration-management or hardening tools applying immutable file attributes
// References:
//   - https://isc.sans.edu/diary/30950
//   - https://www.akamai.com/blog/security-research/dhpcd-cryptominer-hid-four-years
//   - https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man1/chattr.1.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/8d36168a926cfb3c84681e2e68261e2d69d57ca5/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_ssh_authorized_keys_made_immutable.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "/chattr" or ProcessCommandLine contains "chattr ") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "/.ssh/authorized_keys" and (ProcessCommandLine contains " +i" or ProcessCommandLine contains " +a"))
